    "In the older bungalows, bathrooms are often small and idiosyncratic: a tub on feet or a cast-iron built-in, tile set in mud beds, plumbing that's been rerouted more than once. The temptation is to gut everything; often the smarter move is a surgical update — a new wet area, modern fixtures, better ventilation — that respects the home's character and your budget. Our budget shower renovation, from $9,900, exists precisely for these rooms: new base, composite walls, sliding glass door, new fixtures, done in 2–3 days with no tile and no grout to maintain.",
